1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,150
Most people assume Dubai got rich on

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,030
oil.

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:06,598
Its own government says more than 95

4
00:00:06,598 --> 00:00:09,328
percent of its economy has nothing to

5
00:00:09,328 --> 00:00:10,610
do with oil.

6
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:13,832
So where does the money actually come

7
00:00:13,832 --> 00:00:14,729
from?

8
00:00:14,983 --> 00:00:18,376
This desert city of about 4.6 million

9
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:20,685
people runs the busiest airport in the

10
00:00:20,685 --> 00:00:23,533
world for international passengers.

11
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:25,365
In 2025,

12
00:00:25,365 --> 00:00:29,343
95.2 million passengers passed through it.

13
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:32,540
Dubai sells something harder to see than

14
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:33,051
oil,

15
00:00:33,051 --> 00:00:35,533
and much harder to copy.

16
00:00:35,803 --> 00:00:36,745
To find it,

17
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,411
we will follow the ships,

18
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:39,353
the planes,

19
00:00:39,353 --> 00:00:41,643
the buildings and the rules.

20
00:00:41,843 --> 00:00:43,243
And we will look at who pays

21
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:44,243
the bill.

22
00:00:44,273 --> 00:00:47,020
This is The Hidden Economics.

23
00:00:50,483 --> 00:00:51,001
First,

24
00:00:51,001 --> 00:00:52,963
a common mistake.

25
00:00:52,963 --> 00:00:55,603
Dubai is not a country.

26
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:57,751
It is one of the seven emirates

27
00:00:57,751 --> 00:01:00,563
that form the United Arab Emirates.

28
00:01:00,803 --> 00:01:01,950
Its bigger neighbour,

29
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:02,902
Abu Dhabi,

30
00:01:02,902 --> 00:01:05,057
is the federal capital.

31
00:01:05,317 --> 00:01:08,047
That difference matters.

32
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:10,439
Under the UAE constitution,

33
00:01:10,439 --> 00:01:12,991
each emirate owns its own natural

34
00:01:12,991 --> 00:01:14,247
resources.

35
00:01:14,247 --> 00:01:17,167
And Abu Dhabi holds about 94 percent

36
00:01:17,167 --> 00:01:19,537
of the country's oil reserves.

37
00:01:19,707 --> 00:01:22,754
Dubai holds about 4 percent.

38
00:01:23,017 --> 00:01:26,024
So Dubai never had Abu Dhabi's oil

39
00:01:26,024 --> 00:01:26,827
wealth.

40
00:01:26,827 --> 00:01:29,077
It needed another business model.

41
00:01:29,097 --> 00:01:31,177
To see where that model came from,

42
00:01:31,177 --> 00:01:32,813
we have to go back to a

43
00:01:32,813 --> 00:01:35,049
time before the skyscrapers.

44
00:01:38,483 --> 00:01:40,329
Long before the towers,

45
00:01:40,329 --> 00:01:42,736
Dubai was a small trading town on

46
00:01:42,736 --> 00:01:44,673
a saltwater creek.

47
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:47,359
Its economy floated on pearls,

48
00:01:47,359 --> 00:01:49,911
gathered by divers and sold on to

49
00:01:49,911 --> 00:01:51,531
distant markets.

50
00:01:51,783 --> 00:01:54,323
Then the pearl trade collapsed.

51
00:01:54,323 --> 00:01:57,035
Japan began producing cultured pearls from

52
00:01:57,035 --> 00:01:58,684
1916,

53
00:01:58,684 --> 00:02:01,938
and the crash of 1929 finished what

54
00:02:01,938 --> 00:02:04,120
was left of the old market.

55
00:02:04,383 --> 00:02:07,447
But Dubai had already learned a different

56
00:02:07,447 --> 00:02:08,283
trick.

57
00:02:08,363 --> 00:02:11,144
In the years after 1902,

58
00:02:11,144 --> 00:02:13,835
as the Persian port of Lingeh declined,

59
00:02:13,835 --> 00:02:16,074
merchants moved across the water,

60
00:02:16,074 --> 00:02:18,335
and Dubai became the main trading centre

61
00:02:18,335 --> 00:02:19,613
of its coast.

62
00:02:19,983 --> 00:02:22,304
Its advantage was openness,

63
00:02:22,304 --> 00:02:24,730
not natural resources.

64
00:02:24,983 --> 00:02:27,116
In 1959,

65
00:02:27,116 --> 00:02:29,146
Dubai borrowed money,

66
00:02:29,146 --> 00:02:30,919
largely from Kuwait,

67
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:32,974
to dredge its silting creek so that

68
00:02:32,974 --> 00:02:35,373
bigger ships could reach the town.

69
00:02:35,653 --> 00:02:38,447
It was investing in trade infrastructure

70
00:02:38,447 --> 00:02:40,733
before it had found any oil at

71
00:02:40,733 --> 00:02:41,587
all.

72
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:47,454
In 1966,

73
00:02:47,454 --> 00:02:49,452
oil was finally found,

74
00:02:49,452 --> 00:02:50,292
offshore,

75
00:02:50,292 --> 00:02:52,340
in the Fateh field.

76
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:56,428
The first cargo left in 1969.

77
00:02:56,683 --> 00:02:59,752
But Dubai's oil was never going to

78
00:02:59,752 --> 00:03:00,533
last.

79
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:04,337
Production peaked in 1991 and has declined

80
00:03:04,337 --> 00:03:05,593
ever since.

81
00:03:05,703 --> 00:03:07,745
The money it did earn went into

82
00:03:07,745 --> 00:03:09,605
things more permanent than wells:

83
00:03:09,605 --> 00:03:10,036
roads,

84
00:03:10,036 --> 00:03:11,148
a modern port,

85
00:03:11,148 --> 00:03:11,579
and,

86
00:03:11,579 --> 00:03:14,142
opened in 1979,

87
00:03:14,142 --> 00:03:17,011
a vast new harbour at Jebel Ali.

88
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:20,110
That is the first key to Dubai.

89
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:22,380
Oil was not the business.

90
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:24,246
It was the seed money for a

91
00:03:24,246 --> 00:03:26,743
business built on moving other people's

92
00:03:26,743 --> 00:03:27,570
goods.

93
00:03:31,017 --> 00:03:32,547
Look at the map.

94
00:03:32,547 --> 00:03:35,570
Dubai sits between the factories of Asia,

95
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:38,147
the consumers of Europe and the growing

96
00:03:38,147 --> 00:03:40,387
markets of East Africa.

97
00:03:40,527 --> 00:03:42,121
Ships can unload here,

98
00:03:42,121 --> 00:03:44,552
and goods can be shipped on across

99
00:03:44,552 --> 00:03:46,503
the whole region.

100
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:48,003
Next to the port,

101
00:03:48,003 --> 00:03:51,047
Dubai created the Jebel Ali Free Zone,

102
00:03:51,047 --> 00:03:53,540
in 1985.

103
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:56,560
It started with nineteen companies.

104
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:59,303
Today it hosts more than 11,000

105
00:03:59,303 --> 00:04:00,647
businesses.

106
00:04:00,883 --> 00:04:02,913
In 2024,

107
00:04:02,913 --> 00:04:06,289
the zone handled 713 billion dirhams of

108
00:04:06,289 --> 00:04:07,623
non-oil trade.

109
00:04:07,763 --> 00:04:10,033
By the Dubai government's own estimate,

110
00:04:10,033 --> 00:04:11,940
the zone and the port together account

111
00:04:11,940 --> 00:04:14,649
for about 36 percent of the emirate's

112
00:04:14,649 --> 00:04:16,012
economy.

113
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:19,782
Jebel Ali handled about 15.6 million

114
00:04:19,782 --> 00:04:20,627
containers,

115
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:24,375
measured in twenty-foot units in 2025,

116
00:04:24,375 --> 00:04:26,541
which made it the ninth busiest container

117
00:04:26,541 --> 00:04:27,603
port in the world,

118
00:04:27,603 --> 00:04:29,503
according to Lloyd's List.

119
00:04:29,750 --> 00:04:32,211
And the company that runs it,

120
00:04:32,211 --> 00:04:33,012
DP World,

121
00:04:33,012 --> 00:04:36,930
is no longer just Dubai's port operator.

122
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:39,005
It is a global business,

123
00:04:39,005 --> 00:04:41,157
owned by the Dubai government,

124
00:04:41,157 --> 00:04:44,483
that reported 24.4 billion dollars of

125
00:04:44,483 --> 00:04:47,126
revenue in 2025.

126
00:04:50,583 --> 00:04:53,733
Aviation followed the same logic.

127
00:04:53,783 --> 00:04:57,545
Emirates was launched in 1985 with about

128
00:04:57,545 --> 00:05:00,998
10 million dollars and two leased planes.

129
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:03,850
The pitch was geography.

130
00:05:03,950 --> 00:05:05,814
Dubai says a third of the world's

131
00:05:05,814 --> 00:05:08,378
population lives within four hours' flight

132
00:05:08,378 --> 00:05:09,910
of its airport.

133
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:12,754
So instead of flying people to Dubai,

134
00:05:12,754 --> 00:05:15,538
Emirates could fly them through it.

135
00:05:15,783 --> 00:05:17,423
It worked.

136
00:05:17,423 --> 00:05:19,484
In its latest financial year,

137
00:05:19,484 --> 00:05:22,773
the Emirates Group made 21 billion dirhams

138
00:05:22,773 --> 00:05:24,371
of profit after tax,

139
00:05:24,371 --> 00:05:28,653
on revenue of 150.5 billion dirhams.

140
00:05:28,753 --> 00:05:30,316
And it paid its owner,

141
00:05:30,316 --> 00:05:32,786
a Dubai government investment fund,

142
00:05:32,786 --> 00:05:36,490
a dividend of 3.5 billion dirhams.

143
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:39,465
Dubai's airport is already full of

144
00:05:39,465 --> 00:05:40,880
ambition.

145
00:05:40,910 --> 00:05:44,160
The city has approved a 128 billion

146
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:46,137
dirhams terminal at Al Maktoum

147
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,433
International,

148
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:50,902
designed for up to 260 million passengers

149
00:05:50,902 --> 00:05:51,942
a year.

150
00:05:55,383 --> 00:05:58,423
All those flights fill hotels.

151
00:05:58,513 --> 00:06:02,285
Dubai received 19.6 million international

152
00:06:02,285 --> 00:06:05,233
overnight visitors in 2025,

153
00:06:05,233 --> 00:06:09,005
and average hotel occupancy reached 80.7

154
00:06:09,005 --> 00:06:10,018
percent.

155
00:06:10,283 --> 00:06:12,058
Then there is property,

156
00:06:12,058 --> 00:06:14,973
the most visible engine of all.

157
00:06:15,103 --> 00:06:17,301
In 2025,

158
00:06:17,301 --> 00:06:19,949
real estate transactions in Dubai were

159
00:06:19,949 --> 00:06:22,782
worth 917 billion dirhams,

160
00:06:22,782 --> 00:06:26,771
up from 761 billion the year before.

161
00:06:27,017 --> 00:06:29,607
The state is never far away.

162
00:06:29,747 --> 00:06:30,359
Emaar,

163
00:06:30,359 --> 00:06:32,869
the city's biggest listed developer,

164
00:06:32,869 --> 00:06:34,113
counts Dubai Holding,

165
00:06:34,113 --> 00:06:35,780
a government-owned group,

166
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:38,067
as its largest shareholder.

167
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:40,226
And buyers mostly pay cash:

168
00:06:40,226 --> 00:06:43,071
the IMF found that about 83 percent

169
00:06:43,071 --> 00:06:46,982
of home purchases in 2024 used no

170
00:06:46,982 --> 00:06:48,090
mortgage.

171
00:06:48,350 --> 00:06:50,400
Prices have soared.

172
00:06:50,470 --> 00:06:51,970
According to the IMF,

173
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:54,145
villa prices more than doubled between

174
00:06:54,145 --> 00:06:59,050
early 2020 and the middle of 2025.

175
00:07:02,517 --> 00:07:06,247
Dubai's other export is its rulebook.

176
00:07:06,247 --> 00:07:08,395
The emirate has more than 20 free

177
00:07:08,395 --> 00:07:08,952
zones,

178
00:07:08,952 --> 00:07:10,870
where foreign companies can be wholly

179
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:12,237
foreign-owned.

180
00:07:12,417 --> 00:07:14,352
And Since 2021,

181
00:07:14,352 --> 00:07:16,641
full foreign ownership has been allowed

182
00:07:16,641 --> 00:07:19,321
for most businesses outside them too.

183
00:07:19,583 --> 00:07:20,696
In finance,

184
00:07:20,696 --> 00:07:22,723
Dubai went further.

185
00:07:22,883 --> 00:07:24,828
In 2004,

186
00:07:24,828 --> 00:07:27,407
it created the Dubai International

187
00:07:27,407 --> 00:07:28,555
Financial Centre,

188
00:07:28,555 --> 00:07:30,875
a zone with its own English-language,

189
00:07:30,875 --> 00:07:32,413
common-law courts.

190
00:07:32,523 --> 00:07:35,082
By the end of 2025,

191
00:07:35,082 --> 00:07:38,717
it had 8,844 active companies.

192
00:07:38,983 --> 00:07:40,054
And taxes,

193
00:07:40,054 --> 00:07:41,675
long close to zero,

194
00:07:41,675 --> 00:07:43,923
are no longer zero.

195
00:07:44,133 --> 00:07:46,857
Most companies now pay 9 percent corporate

196
00:07:46,857 --> 00:07:51,263
tax on profits above 375,000 dirhams.

197
00:07:51,413 --> 00:07:53,837
Qualifying free-zone companies can still

198
00:07:53,837 --> 00:07:57,103
pay zero percent on qualifying income.

199
00:07:57,263 --> 00:08:00,496
Large multinationals face a 15 percent

200
00:08:00,496 --> 00:08:01,697
minimum tax,

201
00:08:01,697 --> 00:08:04,048
and VAT of 5 percent applies to

202
00:08:04,048 --> 00:08:05,383
most spending.

203
00:08:05,583 --> 00:08:08,073
Individuals still pay no income tax on

204
00:08:08,073 --> 00:08:09,579
their salaries.

205
00:08:09,817 --> 00:08:11,303
Put it all together,

206
00:08:11,303 --> 00:08:13,671
and this is what Dubai's economy looks

207
00:08:13,671 --> 00:08:14,917
like today.

208
00:08:15,027 --> 00:08:16,633
Trade is the largest slice,

209
00:08:16,633 --> 00:08:18,704
at about a fifth of output,

210
00:08:18,704 --> 00:08:20,310
followed by finance,

211
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:22,307
real estate and transport.

212
00:08:22,437 --> 00:08:24,640
Oil is a small part of everything

213
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,460
else.

214
00:08:28,917 --> 00:08:31,905
This model runs on people from somewhere

215
00:08:31,905 --> 00:08:32,777
else.

216
00:08:32,967 --> 00:08:35,101
Human Rights Watch says migrant workers

217
00:08:35,101 --> 00:08:37,519
make up 88 percent of the UAE's

218
00:08:37,519 --> 00:08:39,067
population.

219
00:08:39,297 --> 00:08:41,291
They build the towers,

220
00:08:41,291 --> 00:08:44,934
staff the hotels and drive the city.

221
00:08:45,183 --> 00:08:48,252
The group has documented recruitment fees,

222
00:08:48,252 --> 00:08:49,515
unpaid wages,

223
00:08:49,515 --> 00:08:51,553
and a sponsorship system,

224
00:08:51,553 --> 00:08:53,074
known as kafala,

225
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:55,137
that ties workers' visas to their

226
00:08:55,137 --> 00:08:56,253
employers.

227
00:08:56,453 --> 00:09:00,138
The labour ministry handled 46,819

228
00:09:00,138 --> 00:09:03,593
unpaid-wage cases in 2022.

229
00:09:03,783 --> 00:09:06,254
The government points to measures such as

230
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:08,276
a summer ban on outdoor work from

231
00:09:08,276 --> 00:09:09,849
half past twelve to three in the

232
00:09:09,849 --> 00:09:11,123
afternoon.

233
00:09:11,373 --> 00:09:13,869
Human Rights Watch says that is not

234
00:09:13,869 --> 00:09:15,093
enough.

235
00:09:15,350 --> 00:09:18,090
The second risk is debt.

236
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,737
When the global financial crisis hit,

237
00:09:20,737 --> 00:09:24,130
Dubai property prices fell by about half.

238
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:27,101
In November 2009,

239
00:09:27,101 --> 00:09:29,913
Dubai asked creditors of Dubai World,

240
00:09:29,913 --> 00:09:32,016
a state-owned conglomerate,

241
00:09:32,016 --> 00:09:34,663
for a pause on about 26 billion

242
00:09:34,663 --> 00:09:36,209
dollars of debt.

243
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:39,359
Abu Dhabi stepped in with 10 billion

244
00:09:39,359 --> 00:09:40,400
dollars.

245
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:41,454
Weeks later,

246
00:09:41,454 --> 00:09:44,132
in January 2010,

247
00:09:44,132 --> 00:09:46,478
the world's tallest tower opened,

248
00:09:46,478 --> 00:09:48,611
and its name changed from Burj Dubai

249
00:09:48,611 --> 00:09:50,010
to Burj Khalifa,

250
00:09:50,010 --> 00:09:52,505
after Abu Dhabi's ruler.

251
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:53,464
Today,

252
00:09:53,464 --> 00:09:55,682
the IMF warns that a reversal of

253
00:09:55,682 --> 00:09:56,889
capital flows,

254
00:09:56,889 --> 00:09:59,574
or a shift in investor sentiment,

255
00:09:59,574 --> 00:10:01,791
could trigger an unexpected price

256
00:10:01,791 --> 00:10:03,130
correction.

257
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:05,770
It also notes that the finances of

258
00:10:05,770 --> 00:10:08,170
government-related companies are hard to

259
00:10:08,170 --> 00:10:08,750
assess,

260
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:10,951
because the data are not published in

261
00:10:10,951 --> 00:10:11,751
full.

262
00:10:12,017 --> 00:10:14,547
Then came a real test.

263
00:10:14,647 --> 00:10:16,698
A regional war broke out at the

264
00:10:16,698 --> 00:10:19,502
end of February 2026,

265
00:10:19,502 --> 00:10:21,697
disrupting travel and trade.

266
00:10:21,797 --> 00:10:23,704
In the first half of the year,

267
00:10:23,704 --> 00:10:27,494
Dubai's economy was 2.3 percent smaller

268
00:10:27,494 --> 00:10:29,301
than a year earlier.

269
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:36,150
So how does Dubai really make money?

270
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,020
Not mainly from oil.

271
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:40,259
It makes money by being the place

272
00:10:40,259 --> 00:10:41,294
in between:

273
00:10:41,294 --> 00:10:42,502
where goods change ships,

274
00:10:42,502 --> 00:10:44,203
passengers change planes,

275
00:10:44,203 --> 00:10:46,914
capital finds a home and companies set

276
00:10:46,914 --> 00:10:49,240
up under rules they trust.

277
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:50,777
The state builds the hub,

278
00:10:50,777 --> 00:10:52,870
through companies it owns.

279
00:10:52,870 --> 00:10:56,016
Foreign money and foreign workers fill it.

280
00:10:56,250 --> 00:10:58,729
That model has proved remarkably

281
00:10:58,729 --> 00:11:00,320
adaptable.

282
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:02,923
It survived the end of pearling,

283
00:11:02,923 --> 00:11:04,841
the decline of oil and the debt

284
00:11:04,841 --> 00:11:05,920
crisis.

285
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,744
Its own plan aims to double the

286
00:11:07,744 --> 00:11:10,900
size of the economy within a decade.

287
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:13,770
But it depends on flows Dubai does

288
00:11:13,770 --> 00:11:14,950
not control:

289
00:11:14,950 --> 00:11:16,047
